Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 14:00:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 206/209] feat(area): spline smoothing and rotation-minimizing
 frames

Two additions to the spline shape, both defaulting to the legacy behaviour so
that existing content keeps its silhouette exactly.

1. SMOOTHING. SmoothIterations (0-4, default 0) subdivides the control polygon
before the Bezier is fitted, and Tension (0-1, default 1) scales the derived
handle lengths - 1 is legacy's lenB/lenOsn/3 unchanged, 0 collapses the curve
onto its control polygon.

The scheme is the 4-point INTERPOLATING subdivision (Dyn-Levin-Gregory, the
subdivision form of a Catmull-Rom), not Chaikin. Chaikin corner-cutting is
approximating: after one pass none of the authored points is on the curve and
the whole shape shrinks inwards, which is the wrong trade when those points are
what the user drags. The 4-point rule keeps every authored point on the curve
and only inserts one point per edge at (-p0 + 9p1 + 9p2 - p3)/16. That choice
also buys the exact mapping the tools need: each pass doubles the edges, so
authored point i is evaluation point i * 2^n, and GetEdgePoints() hands the tool
the run of evaluation segments an authored edge became. The point tool therefore
still edits the original points, and Ctrl+click still inserts on the drawn curve.

Smoothing is an EVALUATION transform, never a data change: m_points is
untouched, and the cache grows an evaluation polygon that everything downstream
- handles, samples, arc length, contour, hit test, previewer - reads instead.
Angle and Width are subdivided in lockstep with the positions so the per-point
attributes keep meaning; the "use the consumer's width" flag becomes a negative
sentinel inside the cache. Samples per segment halve with each pass, so the
contour buffer and the drawing cost stay roughly constant. The previewer draws
the control polygon faintly whenever smoothing is on, so both are visible.

2. ROTATION-MINIMIZING FRAMES. FrameMode { LegacyUp (default), ParallelTransport }.

Legacy's normal is Vec3(0,0,1).Cross(tangent) - SplineMath::SegmentNormal, from
CSplineObject::GetLocalBezierNormal (SplineObject.cpp:874 and :880). As the
tangent approaches world up that cross product's LENGTH goes to zero, so its
direction is decided by whatever horizontal component is left and swings through
half a turn as the curve passes vertical. Everything oriented by it spins - which
is what the user saw as distributed models rotating along the curve.

ParallelTransport carries one normal along the sampled curve with the double
reflection of Wang, Juttler, Zheng and Liu (2008): no preferred up vector, so it
turns only as much as the curve does. It is seeded from legacy's own normal, so
a flat spline is identical in both modes and only curves legacy cannot orient
change. The per-point Angle is applied on top with legacy's own blend, so
switching mode never loses authored banking. The known price, written into the
header: a closed curve's frame does not generally close on itself, so a closed
spline can show one twist at its seam.

